-- title:
--   Tame chart rung: crossing thickness mw descends to m
-- statement:
--   Let $A_2 \to A_1$ be a module-finite algebra of Noetherian commutative rings with $A_1$ a domain and $A_2 \to A_1$ injective, and let a finite group $G$ act faithfully on $A_1$ by ring automorphisms commuting with the $A_2$-action and with $A_2$ the ring of invariants (`Algebra.IsInvariant`). Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $A_1$, $\mathfrak p$ a prime of $A_2$ with $y \cap A_2 = \mathfrak p$. Let $W_2$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal), $\pi \in W_2$ irreducible, and $m, w \ge 1$ with $m$ and $w$ units in $W_2$; assume the inertia group `y.inertia G` has cardinality $w$ and is cyclic. Let $O$ be a localisation of $A_2$ at $\mathfrak p$ equipped with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ from the adic completion $\widehat O$ onto $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W_2)/(X_0X_1 - \pi^{mw})$, and let $S$ be a localisation of $A_1$ at $y$ such that $\widehat S$ is an integrally closed domain and such that, for the composite $A_2$-algebra structure on $S$, $S$ is unramified over $A_2$ at every non-maximal prime; assume further that whenever $\mathfrak p \le y \cap A_2$ the residue extension $(A_1/y)/(A_2/\mathfrak p)$ is separable. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : W_2 \to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma\pi$, and a ring isomorphism $e : \widehat S \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W)/(X_0X_1 - (\sigma\pi)^m)$, compatible with constants from $A_2$: for $b \in A_2$ and $w_0 \in W_2$, if $e_O$ sends the image of $b$ in $\widehat O$ to the class of the constant power series $w_0$, then $e$ sends the image of $b$ in $\widehat S$ to the class of the constant power series $\sigma w_0$.
--
--   This is the chart-level form of the tame step for crossing models: a tame extension with cyclic inertia of order $w$ above a node of thickness $mw$ becomes, after completion, a node of thickness $m$ over possibly enlarged coefficients, in the spirit of Abhyankar's lemma. It is used in the analysis of the completed local rings of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve at supersingular crossing points, via [`ModularCurve.XOneGammaZeroP.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_tame`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneGammaZeroP.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_tame).
